This appears to be the usual oblivious security team overreach and the
person forwarding the questions does not know what they imply. Pen test and
code review reports are sensitive information. Details of system structure
in public enable attacks. Security teams ask regularly for data that they
themselves would not share.

Audit, disclosure procedures, sure, detail of certifications, yes, but
non-commercial OSS projects do not in general do that. Microsoft?s
distribution of R might help with these issues and if it is current might
have enough security procedures around it to deal with some of the security
team requirements.  I think Oracle has a distribution of their own and that
may help with that too but I don?t know how live they both are. Support for
either of those of it is available is likely to cost money.

